        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Read a Z SQL Method of the SQL catalog (its src, arguments_src, connection_id, title and filter metadata).\n
\n
Catalog methods live at portal_catalog/<sql_catalog_id>/<method_id> (e.g.\n
portal_catalog/erp5_mysql_innodb/z_catalog_product_sale_supply_line_list) — NOT on\n
portal_catalog itself: restricted getattr there reports them MISSING. This tool\n
resolves the right container through the trusted MCPDevHelpers\n
(catalogMethodInfo), so a catalog session starts with one read instead of a\n
trusted-code bootstrap.\n
\n
Returns: method_id, sql_catalog_id, title, connection_id, src, arguments_src,\n
filtered, expression, expression_cache_key, filter_portal_types, registrations\n
(which sql_*_list registrations mention the method), and an editing hint.\n
Use erp5_catalog_method_write to patch (src and arguments_src travel together\n
through one manage_edit, which re-parses _arg).

]]></string> </value>
